+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Whether it was deliberate stayed unknown.
+
+On 2026-09-11 the owner requested that both forms of the veterinarian directory narrow to one named specialty. That request touches NG-9, and a request alone never reopens a row. The owner decided the row at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Narrowing the directory by specialty stays out of scope.
+2. **Retire NG-9 for veterinarians.** Any veterinarian search, free text included, becomes buildable.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen by the owner). Free-text veterinarian search stays out; narrowing the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed. Its veterinarian clause now declines free-text search only. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows is in scope. The pet and visit clauses are unchanged.
+
+The owner stated no reason beyond the decision itself, and this record adds none.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- REQ-VET-003 becomes buildable: both forms of the directory narrow to one named specialty.
+- Free-text veterinarian search still requires a new owner decision.
+- Whether a shown attribute other than specialty qualifies is not decided here; a request for one returns to the owner.
+- The veterinarian clause is decided and leaves the open provenance consultation. The pet and visit clauses remain part of it.
+- The narrowing brings no page control with it. The owner scoped REQ-VET-003 to the address alone; a visible control is a separate request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and preamble.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the first capability the narrowing admits.
