+# Specialty Narrowing Runs as an Uncached Repository Query
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+REQ-VET-003 narrows both forms of the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one specialty named in the address. The name is caller-supplied free text.
+
+Every existing `VetRepository` read is cached in the `vets` cache. The cache is keyed by each read's arguments and has no size bound or eviction configured.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Filter in memory over the cached full list.** The controller narrows and pages the cached unfiltered result. The cache is reused, but the matching rule and the paging arithmetic land in a web controller.
+2. **Cached derived repository query.** This matches the other `VetRepository` reads. The caller-supplied name becomes a cache key, so any caller can add entries to an unbounded cache.
+3. **Uncached derived repository query** (chosen). The database matches the whole name ignoring case and pages the result. Nothing is retained per request.
+
+## Decision
+
+Specialty narrowing is a Spring Data derived query on `VetRepository`, one paged and one whole, following the owner search's paged derived query. Neither carries a cache annotation. The unfiltered reads stay cached.
+
+Option 1 fails the Web controller row of the architecture brief, which admits no business rule in a controller. Option 2 lets a request-derived value grow retained memory without limit. A narrowed request costs one query, which a directory of this size absorbs.
+
+The query folds letter case on both sides of the comparison on every vendor. It never relies on column collation, which differs per vendor and already makes owner search case-sensitive on PostgreSQL.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed request always reaches the database; only unfiltered reads benefit from the cache.
+- A later narrowing by another shown attribute follows the same rule: the narrowing value never keys the `vets` cache.
+- Narrowed reads never serve stale data, whatever the answer to the open vet-cache invalidation question.
+- The unfiltered paged read still caches every requested page number. That exposure predates this decision and is recorded in the threat model.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the `VetRepository` row and the vet-cache invariant
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) — the caller-chosen cache-key row
+- [Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In Scope](2026-09-11-non-goal-veterinarian-search-narrowed.md) — the non-goal narrowing that admits REQ-VET-003
